-- Canonical development seed: the single source of seed data for local dev.
--
-- `make api` applies this file automatically, but only to an empty database
-- (no rows in users or parks), so it runs once on first startup and never
-- clobbers local data. To re-apply it to an existing database, run `make seed`.
--
-- Contributors: add or edit rows freely. Keep every statement idempotent (fixed
-- ids plus ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING) so `make seed` stays safe to re-run. The file
-- is applied in a single transaction, so any error rolls back the whole seed.

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

